<%# Article-history pilot: one covered article, in reading order. The article's number always stands first and stays
    where it is (the owner, via Sol 2026-11-23 04:31:08Z: the page jumped at every step; the history box stood above the
    number and pushed it down). While the article shows its plain text, the number is the first word of that text, as
    in every other article. As soon as it shows anything else (its history panel, a wording the reader chose, a
    comparison, the notes an archive date needs, or no wording at all) the number stands on a line of its own
    (laws/_history_identifier), at that same place, and below it, in this order: the panel, the notes, the chosen
    wording's period (while the panel is closed: open, its list of dates shows the period, which stands once; the
    owner, via Sol 2026-11-23 14:13:13Z), and the text. So opening the panel, a step to another wording, a comparison and Close change only
    what stands below the number, and a date switch changes only what stands below the panel.

    The legal text is print_article's output untouched: the live row on the current-law page (live: [text, title,
    type]), else the wording the archive gives or the reader chose. Below the number's own line the text is shown
    without its leading number (hidden by the stylesheet, [data-history-shown-text]); with a comparison, the same
    text carries the change against the wording before (laws/_history_diff), and at the oldest wording there is none,
    so the text stays with a short note. In both cases #article-text-<permalink> (what the copy actions read) is the whole wording,
    kept hidden for the copy (utils/article_copy.js lays it out for the moment of the read). Right after Close,
    data-history-return-focus asks for the focus back on the number (history_links_controller.js).
    Locals: history (HistoryPilotHelper::ArticleState), permalink, numac, live (optional). %>
<% key = history.key %>
<% live = local_assigns[:live] %>
<% open = history_open?(key) %>
<% printed = if history.live? && live
               print_article(*live, source_numac: numac)
             elsif history.shown_body
               print_article(history.shown_body, key, 'ART', source_numac: numac)
             end %>
<% comparing = @history_compare.include?(key) && history.shown_body %>
<% plain = printed && !open && !history.chosen && !comparing && (history.live? || !history.unresolved?) %>
<div data-history-row="<%= key %>" data-history-state="<%= history_rendered_state(key) %>" <%= tag.attributes(data: { history_return_focus: ('' if history_focus?(key, 'close')) }) %>>
  <%= render 'laws/history_link', history: history, permalink: permalink %>
  <% if plain %>
    <div id="article-text-<%= permalink %>"><%= printed %></div>
  <% else %>
    <%= render 'laws/history_identifier', identifier: history_identifier(key) %>
    <% if open %><%= render 'laws/history_picker', history: history, permalink: permalink %><% end %>
    <% unless history.live? %><%= render 'laws/history_notes', history: history %><% end %>
    <% if history.chosen && !open %>
      <p class="not-prose mb-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300" data-history-chosen="<%= key %>"><%= (history_label(:version_label) % { period: history_period(history.selected) }).upcase_first %><% if history.off_date %> (<%= history_label(:off_date) % { date: history_day(@history_as_of) } %>)<% end %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% if comparing && !history.compare_base %>
      <p class="not-prose mb-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300" data-history-no-previous><%= history_label(:no_previous) %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% if comparing && history.compare_base %>
      <%= render 'laws/history_diff', key: key, old_body: history.compare_base.body, new_body: history.shown_body, numac: numac,
                                      notes_only: history.selected&.change_kind == 'notes only' %>
    <% elsif printed %>
      <div data-history-shown-text><%= printed %></div>
    <% end %>
    <%# No wording on the archive date (a gap): the number alone keeps History at hand; the menu then offers no copy of
        a wording that is not there (Sol 2026-11-21 10:09:36Z). %>
    <% if printed %><div id="article-text-<%= permalink %>" hidden data-history-copy-text><%= printed %></div><% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
